==English==

===Etymology===
Latin - "the thing that has been judged"

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[res]] [[judicata]]|pl='''[[res judicatae]]'''}}

# {{law}} An issue that is before a court and has already been decided by another court, thus the current court must dismiss it.

